    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0794" n="784" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg784"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">846G.2393/6–249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-02T12:00:00+08:00">June 2,
                            1949—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received June 3—2:35 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 519. Central Bank requesting Embassy office explore possibility US
                    military airlift to Hong Kong at “nominal” cost 5 million silver dollars being
                    minted at Philadelphia for Chinese Government. Airlift to be completed
                    mid-June.</p>
                <p>Central Bank claims commercial airlift costs prohibitive and delivery urgent for
                    purpose expedite introduction new currency program.</p>
                <p>Would appreciate instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
